<title>USA: MAXIMUS wins $26 mln Milwaukee contract.</title>
<headline>MAXIMUS wins $26 mln Milwaukee contract.</headline>
<dateline>MILWAUKEE 1997-08-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>MAXIMUS Inc said it had won a $26 million contract to provide welfare-to-work services in Milwaukee County, beginning September 1.</p>
<p>The initial contract term was 28 months, the company said.</p>
<p>The contract was awarded to the company under the 1996 Welfare Reform Act, MAXIMUS said.</p>
<p>MAXIMUS says it is the largest health and human services management firm in the United States.</p>
</text>
